# The bytes in the repository are the bytes you get.  Git for Windows ships with
# core.autocrlf=true in its system config, which turns every text file into CRLF
# on checkout -- that alone made a fresh clone fail the protocol suite, because
# examples/hello.bf comes back 841 bytes instead of 820 and the fixtures are
# compared byte for byte.  Pinning LF here makes a clone on any machine
# identical to the one the tests were written against.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Not text, whatever the extension suggests: a checkout must not touch these.
*.png binary
*.exe binary
*.ico binary
